# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repo is FOR: the playable build, the docs, and everything needed to
# rebuild the playable build. Not the asset masters.
#
# The paintings and the recordings are already INSIDE index.html - the art as
# base64 PNG, the music and sfx as base64 AAC. Committing the sources as well
# would put ~360MB of PNG and WAV into every clone to ship a 10MB page. They
# live in the Google Drive folder, which is where the pipeline reads them from.
#
# If a source folder here ever needs to be in git, take it out one folder at a
# time and say why - do not delete this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# painting masters, 130MB. build_assets.ps1 + inject.ps1 turn these into the
# base64 block in the prototype; the block is committed, the PNGs are not.
art/src/
art/out/

# the woff2 cache, 479KB. Same rule as the paintings and for the same reason:
# build_fonts.py + inject_fonts.ps1 turn these into the base64 @font-face block
# in the prototype, and THAT is what ships and is committed. `--fetch` pulls
# them again from scratch, so nothing here is unrecoverable. The SCRIPT is in
# git precisely so the face list, the subsets and the licences are reviewable
# without the binaries.
art/fonts/src/

# the approved 44.1k WAV pack, 79MB, and its encoded derivatives.
# build_audio.ps1 turns these into audio/out/audio_data.js; build_site.ps1
# pours that into index.html.
audio/music/
audio/sfx/
audio/web/
audio/out/

# rejected takes and synthesis previews kept for comparison, 76MB
audio_review/

# scratch: the running game POSTs its own board here to be looked at. It had
# grown to 181MB, so on 2026-08-14 every capture before #133 was deleted and it
# is 1.6MB again. Nothing here is in git, so a deleted shot is gone: the eye
# check is paid at the time, and the rows in SHIPPED.md keep what was measured.
shots/

# a staging copy of painting masters, 17MB, made outside the pipeline. Same rule
# as art/src/ above and for the same reason: the paintings that SHIP are the
# base64 block inside index.html, and several of these files are byte-copies of
# ones already in art/src/ (P1_The_Captain.png, EV-33_ash-at-the-fire.png).
# `deploy.ps1` runs `git add -A`, so without this line the next deploy puts them
# on the live repo - which is the failure the *.gdoc note below already records.
prototype/assets/

# tarball of the docs as they stood before the 2026-07-31 cleanup
_archive_docs_*.tar.gz

# per-machine Claude Code state. .claude/rules/, .claude/skills/ and
# .claude/settings.json ARE tracked: the last one carries the collision hook.
.claude/settings.local.json

# a branch desk's one-line note about what it is for, written by
# tools/branch.ps1 new -t. Per-desk scratch, never repo content.
.desk

# who currently holds which number and which file, written by tools/claim.ps1.
# Deliberately NOT committed: it is live state about the two sessions running on
# this machine right now, and both of them read it off the same disk.
.grimtoll/

__pycache__/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Google Drive shortcut stubs. The repo lives in a Drive folder, so the user's
# own documents sit beside the source - and `deploy.ps1` runs `git add -A`,
# which swept one of them into a deploy commit before this line existed. They
# are pointers, not files: there is nothing in them to version.
*.gdoc
*.gsheet
*.gslides
